    {
      "id": "claim_dca8a1121e974197833865d6aefc4049",
      "statement": "Every HTTP request passes through auth.Manager.Middleware, which is wrapped around the ServeMux once in New, so Handler() is the single entry point.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/server/server.go#L128-L137",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:361f2286d89bbe56466a4d0086386102bd6e170ebe9537f9bf3a98be9c10fce3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_dafa5a7dc04d40478e6216978c32df93",
      "statement": "The auth middleware sorts requests into four cases in order: auth disabled (synthetic local admin user), public API (/api/healthz and the /api/auth/ prefix), SPA shell and assets (served, session user attached when present), and everything else (session required or 401 JSON).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/auth/auth.go#L222-L254",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2094cb8ec083fb508300d67c7769e0ecf4637c55b8301a500f527bf1126e5f18:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_35d48522e64640a6b5e770d54adb2f6b",
      "statement": "An unauthenticated API request is answered with 401, Content-Type application/json and the body {\"error\":\"unauthorized\"}.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/auth/auth.go#L243-L249",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5a8f6fbece2f199ecbc9b8bc9599a8613710fb73776f2b16703807709b795543:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
